*nat
:PREROUTING ACCEPT [0:0]
# Redirect HTTPS from exit-node clients (arriving on tailscale0) to the
# local mitmproxy transparent listener. mitmproxy inspects the TLS SNI
# via a tls_clienthello hook in ad_block.py and passes anything
# non-Discord/non-Reddit straight through as a raw TCP relay — only
# those hostnames get decrypted/filtered. Traffic NOT arriving via
# tailscale0 (i.e. the CT's own outbound traffic) is untouched.
#
# NOTE: DNS is NOT handled here. Exit-node clients' DNS queries never
# transit tailscale0 as real UDP/TCP:53 packets (Tailscale tunnels them
# internally), so a PREROUTING DNAT rule for port 53 is a structural
# no-op — confirmed via tcpdump (zero packets matched during active
# client DNS traffic). DNS-level ad blocking for exit-node clients is
# instead handled by pointing this CT's OWN /etc/resolv.conf at AdGuard
# Home (see the "DNS-level ad/tracker blocking" section in tasks/main.yml).
-A PREROUTING -i tailscale0 -p tcp --dport 443 -j REDIRECT --to-port 8443

# Also redirect plain HTTP (port 80). Needed specifically so
# http://mitm.it (the cert-install page, visited BEFORE the device
# trusts anything) actually gets intercepted — mitmproxy special-cases
# that exact request and serves its own install page instead of
# proxying it through. Without this rule the phone's HTTP request to
# mitm.it just reaches the real internet unmodified (confirmed
# 2026-07-27: phone got the real mitm.it site, which literally says
# "If you can see this, traffic is not going through mitmproxy").
# Plain HTTP needs no cert trust to intercept (nothing is encrypted),
# and ad_block.py's request() hook already no-ops on any non-Discord/
# non-Reddit host, so this is safe for the same reason the HTTPS
# SNI-passthrough is safe.
-A PREROUTING -i tailscale0 -p tcp --dport 80 -j REDIRECT --to-port 8443
COMMIT

*filter
:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
# Restrict the CT's OWN outbound traffic (i.e. traffic this box
# originates itself — logging, health checks, package updates) to
# exactly what it needs. This is DISTINCT from exit-node relay traffic,
# which flows through the FORWARD chain (ts-forward, tagged by the
# Tailscale-managed fwmark) and is untouched by anything here — an exit
# node's whole job is relaying arbitrary internet traffic on behalf of
# clients, so OUTPUT restrictions only bound what THIS HOST can reach on
# its own behalf. Concern: adblock-proxy-01 sits with a foot on both the
# private SDN (172.16.0.0/24 — dns-01, lb-01, proxmox nodes, etc.) and
# the LAN (192.168.86.0/24, for AdGuard/HA) — without this, a compromised
# process here (mitmproxy itself, or the log-shipper cron job) could
# pivot laterally to any private-subnet or LAN host. Locked down
# 2026-07-27 in response to a direct ask: "worried about network lateral
# movement... as long as we lock that down then it's fine to go direct
# and not through tailscale."
-A OUTPUT -o lo -j ACCEPT
-A OUTPUT -m conntrack --ctstate ESTABLISHED,RELATED -j ACCEPT
# Loki push (adguard-log-shipper.sh + Alloy, once this CT joins the
# monitoring fleet).
-A OUTPUT -d {{ ip_vm }} -p tcp --dport 3100 -j ACCEPT
# VictoriaMetrics remote-write (Alloy node_exporter metrics push).
-A OUTPUT -d {{ ip_vm }} -p tcp --dport 8428 -j ACCEPT
# AdGuard Home query log API + Home Assistant core API, both served from
# the same host.
-A OUTPUT -d {{ ip_homeassistant }} -p tcp --dport 8123 -j ACCEPT
-A OUTPUT -d {{ ip_homeassistant }} -p tcp --dport 53 -j ACCEPT
-A OUTPUT -d {{ ip_homeassistant }} -p udp --dport 53 -j ACCEPT
# DNS resolution for this CT's own outbound lookups (apt, tailscale
# control plane, blocklist-adjacent hostnames) — same AdGuard resolver
# already configured in /etc/resolv.conf, covered by the rule above.
# Explicit DROP for the rest of the private SDN and LAN — this is the
# actual lateral-movement lockout. Order matters: these DROPs come
# AFTER the narrow ACCEPTs above, so dns-01/lb-01/proxmox/etc. are
# unreachable but AdGuard+Loki still work.
-A OUTPUT -d {{ net_private_range }} -j DROP
-A OUTPUT -d {{ net_lan_range }} -j DROP
# Everything else (the public internet) stays open — required for the
# CT's own package management, Tailscale control-plane heartbeats, and
# critically the mitmproxy addon's own re-originated connections to real
# Discord/other servers after SNI inspection (those ARE this box acting
# on its own behalf, from mitmproxy's perspective, even though they're
# serving an exit-node client).
-A OUTPUT -j ACCEPT
COMMIT
